# 💻🟢 06 — GLOW Terminal

GLOW stands for **Glowing Logical Operator Window** and gives CyberWriter a vault-aware terminal inside the application.

### ⌨️ Terminal Commands

| 💻 **Command** | 🧠 **Purpose**                  |
| -------------- | ------------------------------- |
| 📂 `ls`        | 📋 List vault content           |
| 🌲 `tree`      | 🗂️ Explore folder structure    |
| 🔎 `grep`      | 🧭 Search content               |
| 🔗 `backlinks` | 🔙 Inspect note connections     |
| 🤖 `ai`        | 🧠 Work with AI from the prompt |
| 👁️ `show <n>` | 🔍 Preview an operation         |
| ❌ `cancel`     | 🛑 Discard a pending plan       |
| ↩️ `undo`      | 🔄 Reverse the last apply       |

### 🔐 GLOW Safety Box

🛡️ **Vault Boundary** — GLOW is restricted to the vault.

🗑️ **Safer Removal** — `rm` moves content to Trash rather than permanently deleting it.

👁️ **Preview First** — Planned operations can be inspected before applying.

↩️ **Rollback** — The latest applied plan can be reverted.

